; Winsock catalog + transport mapping for the netstack (smoltcp) transport.
; Normally written by network setup from media/inf/nettcpip.inf, which the
; LiveCD never runs. Two registry halves are required and BOTH must be present
; or usermode socket() fails:
;
;   (1) Winsock2 protocol catalog  — ws2_32 finds the msafd provider here.
;   (2) Winsock (v1) transport map — msafd!SockGetTdiName reads this to resolve
;       (af,type,protocol) -> TDI device via the wshtcpip helper DLL.
;
; With only (1), ws2_32 reaches msafd, but msafd!SockGetTdiName ->
; SockLoadTransportList reads SYSTEM\...\Services\Winsock\Parameters\Transports,
; finds nothing, and returns WSAEINVAL (10022) — socket() fails before AFD is
; ever contacted. The transport "Tcpip" + wshtcpip.dll mapping below returns the
; TDI names \Device\Tcp \Device\Udp \Device\RawIp, which netstack.sys owns
; (sdk/lib/rust/netstack-rust/src/tdidev.rs). All lines extracted verbatim from
; media/inf/nettcpip.inf.

; --- (2) Winsock (v1) transport mapping: msafd -> wshtcpip -> \Device\Tcp/Udp/RawIp ---
